se function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the domain of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2<x<4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2<{f}^{-1}(x)<4\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179128 :answer-field/correct "answer-0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" "answer-84c08631-0c69-50aa-ad0b-25457d685152" "answer-b1e34b36-ae62-52f5-986a-3b72e39715be" "answer-93dd0e20-404e-5267-89e3-a04adfa86c34" "answer-ee173d36-05ed-5aa9-963b-321b4dde6642"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" :answer/id #uuid "0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c08631-0c69-50aa-ad0b-25457d685152" :answer/id #uuid "84c08631-0c69-50aa-ad0b-25457d685152" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e34b36-ae62-52f5-986a-3b72e39715be" :answer/id #uuid "b1e34b36-ae62-52f5-986a-3b72e39715be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93dd0e20-404e-5267-89e3-a04adfa86c34" :answer/id #uuid "93dd0e20-404e-5267-89e3-a04adfa86c34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee173d36-05ed-5aa9-963b-321b4dde6642" :answer/id #uuid "ee173d36-05ed-5aa9-963b-321b4dde6642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a8a5b01-a34a-5ec4-a40f-b067d49707a5" :question/id #uuid "8a8a5b01-a34a-5ec4-a40f-b067d49707a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-19230" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3d94b4960b926026845ee19493b5a45e46f0858b6c28f0953dee27af92337bdd